{"body":{"text":["There are three levels. The ground is the sessions and their utterances, as they are kept. Knowledge stands on top, briefs written under the rule. Between them stands the elevation: \"the bottom level being the source, the discussions, the top level being the briefs, and this being the intermediate layer\" (23/94). The elevation tells what was said and where, and Knowledge what holds and why, as the session put it (23/90, 23/91)."]},"id":"1M89M6CHQ4HB000","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A **statement** is one sentence written under the rule, saying first what it conveys: \"we consider what it is we want to convey\" (23/98). It honours what it is: \"if they are something to do, if they are a task, if they are an action, they should be named appropriately\" (23/98), so a task is named as the doing, and what was objected to is written as what is held instead, as the session drew it (23/119). Whether one sentence is enough the author asks, though \"I appreciate the idea that it should be\" (23/116); the session allowed a second, for its reason only (23/129)."]},"id":"1M89M6CHQ4HB001","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A statement \"doesn't have such an address\" (23/116); it is reached by its id, as the session drew it (23/115). It points at its ground, the utterances or sentences it rests on, the author's words or the session's (23/80), which components might show by their numbers (23/116)."]},"id":"1M89M6CHQ4HB002","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Every statement has a **status**, where it stands now: open, asked and not decided; proposed, the session's and not taken up; leaning, the author's, inclined to with doubt; settled, decided by the author; closed, no longer holding. These are Knowledge's own marks, with closed beside them, as the session drew them (23/119, 23/135, 23/137). Each status points at what gave it, the utterance of the decision, and so whose it was, as the session drew it (23/129). A statement's history is its versions (23/132)."]},"id":"1M89M6CHQ4HB003","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The elevation gives what, not why, as the session answered: the reasoning, the turns of a talk and the author's state stay in the sessions and in Knowledge (23/93)."]},"id":"1M89M6CHQ4HB004","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}